From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:01:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] uts/rpc: give rpcb_prot.x's kernel arm the lowercase typedefs

Building `strmod/rpcmod` -- which nothing did until the NFS client was wanted
-- fails in the generated header:

    rpcb_prot.h:470: error: unknown type name 'rpcb'
    rpcb_prot.h:471: error: unknown type name 'rp__list'

rpcb_prot.x carries two hand-written arms. The `#ifndef _KERNEL` arm is
rpcgen's own output and declares both spellings of each type; the `#else`
kernel arm is written out by hand in %-passthrough and declares only the
uppercase ones, plus it names one struct differently:

    userland:  struct rpcb;      typedef struct rpcb rpcb;    /* and RPCB */
               struct rp__list;  typedef struct rp__list rpcblist;
    kernel:    struct rpcb;      typedef struct rpcb RPCB;    /* only */
               struct rpcblist;  typedef struct rpcblist RPCBLIST;

The prototypes rpcgen appends after the guard use the *lowercase* names, so
the kernel arm is missing exactly two typedefs. Everything else the appended
block names -- rpcb_rmtcallargs, rpcblist_ptr, rpcb_entry_list and the rest --
the kernel arm already spells correctly.

Adding the two typedefs is the whole fix. It is preferable to guarding the
appended prototypes out of the kernel, which was the first thing tried: the
kernel genuinely uses one of them, `rpc_subr.c` calling xdr_rpcb() when it
talks to rpcbind, so hiding the block only trades "unknown type name" for
"'xdr_rpcb' undeclared".

Both are pure typedefs of structs the kernel arm already defines, so nothing
changes for a build whose rpcgen does not append the block. illumos' own
rpcgen emits each prototype beside its definition and never reaches this;
NetBSD's, which is what a Linux build host has, appends them at the end.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 usr/src/uts/common/rpc/rpcb_prot.x | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/common/rpc/rpcb_prot.x b/usr/src/uts/common/rpc/rpcb_prot.x
index d69838c91b..61f647617a 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/common/rpc/rpcb_prot.x
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/rpc/rpcb_prot.x
@@ -424,6 +424,7 @@ program RPCBPROG {
 %	char *r_owner;			/* owner of the mapping */
 %};
 %typedef struct rpcb RPCB;
+%typedef struct rpcb rpcb;
 %
 %/*
 % * A list of mappings
@@ -433,6 +434,7 @@ program RPCBPROG {
 %	struct rpcblist *rpcb_next;
 %};
 %typedef struct rpcblist RPCBLIST;
+%typedef struct rpcblist rp__list;
 %typedef struct rpcblist *rpcblist_ptr;
 %
 %/*
